  "answer": "The paper 'Dense Passage Retrieval for Open-Domain Question Answering' (arXiv:2004.04906) was downloaded from arXiv (PDF saved to final_runs/run_002/Dense_Passage_Retrieval_2004.04906.pdf). The article contains 5 numbered formulas. The loss function is equation (2): L(q_i, p_i^+, p_{i,1}^-,...,p_{i,n}^-) = -log( exp(sim(q_i,p_i^+)) / (exp(sim(q_i,p_i^+)) + sum_{j=1..n} exp(sim(q_i,p_{i,j}^-))) ), i.e., the negative log-likelihood of the positive passage against the negatives, with sim(q,p)=E_Q(q)^T E_P(p) from equation (1).",
